1
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:06,930
我新编了一个科学笑话  想听吗
I've invented a science joke, would you like to hear it?

2
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:08,120
好啊
Sure.

3
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:12,040
换一个灯泡要多少个爱迪生呢
How many Edisons does it take to screw in a light bulb?

4
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:13,190
几个
How many?

5
00:00:13,190 --> 00:00:15,150
谁管他  他偷了灯泡这个创意
Who cares? He stole the idea

6
00:00:15,150 --> 00:00:17,690
他不配有自己为主题的笑话
and doesn't deserve his own joke.

7
00:00:17,690 --> 00:00:19,250
这是真的吗
Is that really true?

8
00:00:19,250 --> 00:00:21,960
当然  所以你才能知道这是个好笑话
Of course, that's how you know it's a good joke.

9
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:24,960
好笑话就是得寓教于乐
It not only entertains, it informs.

10
00:00:26,340 --> 00:00:27,790
抱歉打扰了
Hey, sorry to interrupt.

11
00:00:27,790 --> 00:00:28,970
巴里
Uh, Barry,

12
00:00:28,970 --> 00:00:31,980
换一个灯泡要多少个爱迪生呢
uh, how many Edisons does it take to screw in a light bulb?

13
00:00:31,980 --> 00:00:35,410
你知道灯泡实际上不是爱迪生发明的吧
Did you know Edison didn't actually invent the light bulb?

14
00:00:31,980 --> 00:00:35,410
爱迪生不算是最早发明人  只能算是改良

15
00:00:37,810 --> 00:00:40,140
你来干嘛  巴里
What do you want, Barry?

16
00:00:40,140 --> 00:00:43,140
来给艾米送一份小小谢礼
Just wanted to drop this off as a little thank you for Amy.

17
00:00:43,150 --> 00:00:44,480
为什么送我礼物
What's this for?

18
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:46,280
你的点子真的帮了我大忙
Your idea really helped me out.

19
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:48,920
我光锥量子化的论文已经发表到网上了
My light-cone quantization paper's online already.

20
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:51,420
反响非常棒
The response has been amazing.

21
00:00:51,420 --> 00:00:52,510
那太好了
Well, that's fascinating.

22
00:00:52,510 --> 00:00:53,890
我迫不及待要去拜读了
I can't wait to read it.

23
00:00:53,890 --> 00:00:55,430
我也是呢
Oh, no, me as well.

24
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:59,810
请发到我电子邮箱sheldon@bazinga.biz
Uh, please e-mail it to sheldon@bazinga.biz.

25
00:00:59,810 --> 00:01:00,980
为什么是.biz[商]吗
Why "Dot-biz"?

26
00:01:00,980 --> 00:01:03,280
因为我一招"商"得你体无完肤
Because I just gave you the business.

27
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:06,950
还因为bazinga.com被人先注册了
And also bazinga.com was taken.

28
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:09,470
好啦  再次谢谢你
Anyway, thanks again.

29
00:01:09,470 --> 00:01:11,890
库伯  去"吃鸡..."蛋吧
Cooper, suck eggs.

30
00:01:13,660 --> 00:01:15,940
你什么时候去帮巴里·克里普奇了
Since when do you help out Barry Kripke?

31
00:01:15,940 --> 00:01:18,320
我最近在思考通过元胞自动机来
Well, I'd been thinking about a cellular automata approach

32
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:19,520
研究神经元连接
to neuronal connectivity,

33
00:01:19,520 --> 00:01:21,370
然后我觉得这可能对弦理论研究
and I thought it might have some interesting applications

34
00:01:21,370 --> 00:01:23,790
有些不错的用途  小忙不值得一提啦
to string theory-- it's not a big deal.

35
00:01:23,790 --> 00:01:25,200
是吗
Oh, really?

36
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:27,740
我研究弦理论走进死胡同那会儿
When I was doing string theory and hit a dead end,

37
00:01:27,740 --> 00:01:29,410
你怎么没想过来帮我呢
why didn't you try to help me?

38
00:01:29,410 --> 00:01:32,450
我有啊  你说生物学家唯一懂的数学
I did-- you said the only math biologists know is

39
00:01:32,450 --> 00:01:34,550
就是如果有三只青蛙  一只跳走了
if you have three frogs and one hops away,

40
00:01:34,550 --> 00:01:37,280
那还剩下两只
that leaves two frogs.

41
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:40,460
还挺有哏的  的确像是我会说的话
That's pretty funny, that does sound like me.

42
00:01:40,460 --> 00:01:41,390
但这也不代表
But that doesn't mean

43
00:01:41,390 --> 00:01:43,190
你就可以去站街边
that you should be standing on street corners

44
00:01:43,190 --> 00:01:46,820
随便男人经过  就把你的计算给人家啊
handing out your math to whatever guy comes along.

45
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:49,600
谢尔顿  我们都是科学家
Sheldon, we're all scientists.

46
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:51,370
我就是帮忙一个同事
I helped out a fellow colleague.

47
00:01:51,370 --> 00:01:52,740
你要不要这么小气
You're being petty.

48
00:01:52,740 --> 00:01:54,380
我小气吗
I'm being petty?

49
00:01:54,380 --> 00:01:57,370
你明知道我跟巴里是职场上宿敌
You know Barry and I have a professional rivalry.

50
00:01:57,370 --> 00:01:59,780
你也听到他说的了  他叫我去"吃鸡..."蛋
You heard him-- he told me to suck eggs.

51
00:01:59,780 --> 00:02:01,680
如果我跟他是朋友  那他就会叫我去
If we were friends, he would have suggested

52
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:03,740
吃些比较令人爽快的东西
I suck something more pleasant.

53
00:02:06,140 --> 00:02:08,180
你笑什么
Why are you laughing?

54
00:02:08,180 --> 00:02:10,290
你是不是学坏了
Did you learn something?

55
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:30,860
生

56
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:30,860
活

57
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:30,860
大

58
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:30,860
爆

59
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:30,860
炸

60
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:30,860
第八季  第十五集

61
00:02:36,540 --> 00:02:37,460
好的  妈
Okay, Ma.

62
00:02:37,460 --> 00:02:39,090
替我跟格莱蒂斯阿姨问好
Say hi to Aunt Gladys.

63
00:02:39,090 --> 00:02:40,360
我也爱你
Yeah, I love you, too.

64
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:41,700
再见
Bye.

65
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:43,310
你妈妈在佛罗里达玩得开心吗
Your mom having fun in Florida?

66
00:02:43,310 --> 00:02:44,530
她很喜欢那里
Mmm, she loves it.

67
00:02:44,530 --> 00:02:46,510
她终于找到个春暖花开  大家都在讨论
She finally found a place where everyone talks about

68
00:02:46,510 --> 00:02:48,720
流了多少汗的地方
how sweaty they are.

69
00:02:49,190 --> 00:02:50,800
总之  她是想我们回她家
Anyway, she wants us to go to the house

70
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:54,430
去看看斯图尔特会不会太"孤单"
and check in on Stuart because he might be "lonely."

71
00:02:54,430 --> 00:02:55,790
她只是人很好嘛
She's just being nice.

72
00:02:55,790 --> 00:02:57,670
我是他宝贝儿子  她怎么就不找人
Well, I'm her son, how come she doesn't send someone

73
00:02:57,670 --> 00:02:59,900
来看看我孤不孤单
to check on me if I'm lonely?

74
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:02,040
因为你有个老婆
Because you have a wife.

75
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:07,980
是没错  可是有时候你下班好晚
Yeah, well, sometimes you work late.

76
00:03:08,850 --> 00:03:10,690
我知道你不喜欢斯图尔特赖在你家
I know you don't like Stuart being in the house,

77
00:03:10,690 --> 00:03:12,000
但他的店马上要重新开张了
but the store's about to reopen,

78
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,680
我相信他很快又能自食其力
I'm sure he'll get back on his feet.

79
00:03:13,680 --> 00:03:14,430
那就太好了
That would be great.

80
00:03:14,430 --> 00:03:17,780
我也非常想跟我妈的关系回到正常
I'd love for things between me and Mom to get back to normal.

81
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:21,480
"正常"这词有点言过其实  但你说是就是吧
Well, normal's a strong word, but sure.

82
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:27,800
-好啊  -好...
- Hey. - Hello.

83
00:03:28,570 --> 00:03:29,600
你还好吧
You okay?

84
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:31,510
如果我还好  我会说  "好!"
If I was okay, I would've said "Hello"

85
00:03:31,510 --> 00:03:34,180
而不是语气很衰的"好..."
and not the much more ominous "Hello."

86
00:03:35,030 --> 00:03:36,160
怎么啦
What's going on?

87
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:37,970
我在生艾米的气
I'm mad at Amy.

88
00:03:37,970 --> 00:03:41,900
她也在你最爱的无袖背心腋下留下汗渍了吗
Did she leave pit stains in your favorite crop top, too?

89
00:03:42,190 --> 00:03:43,890
没有
No.

90
00:03:44,380 --> 00:03:47,830
她帮巴里·克里普奇在线理论上做出突破
She helped Barry Kripke make an advancement in string theory.

91
00:03:47,830 --> 00:03:49,900
听起来挺好的啊
Oh, that sounds like a good thing.

92
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:52,860
照理来说是  可是我已经不研究弦理论了
Well, it would be, except that I left string theory

93
00:03:52,860 --> 00:03:54,860
因为我觉得那是条死路
because I decided it was a dead end.

94
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:56,760
而她背着我
Yeah, and then she went behind my back

95
00:03:56,760 --> 00:03:58,660
跑去帮忙别人证明我错了
to help someone else prove me wrong.

96
00:03:58,660 --> 00:04:00,910
而且还是帮我的宿敌
My rival, no less.

97
00:04:12,070 --> 00:04:14,200
抱歉让你看到了这一幕
I'm sorry you had to see that.

98
00:04:14,730 --> 00:04:17,630
我只遗憾我手边没相机
I'm sorry I didn't have a camera.

99
00:04:17,630 --> 00:04:19,540
她为什么要这么对我呢
Why would she do this to me?

100
00:04:19,540 --> 00:04:22,230
我想她不是故意要惹你生气
Well, I'm sure she didn't upset you on purpose.

101
00:04:22,230 --> 00:04:23,570
而且你不是总说
Besides, aren't you the one who says

102
00:04:23,570 --> 00:04:26,650
没有什么是比让科学进步更重要的吗
there's nothing more important than the advancement of science?

103
00:04:26,650 --> 00:04:28,710
我说的是  没有什么比
No, I said there's nothing more important

104
00:04:28,710 --> 00:04:31,630
"我"让科学进步更重要的
than me advancing science.

105
00:04:31,630 --> 00:04:33,170
好吧  如果我没理解错
All right, well, if I'm understanding this right,

106
00:04:33,170 --> 00:04:35,560
而她也真的只是帮忙了别的科学家
and all she did was help out another scientist,

107
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:38,570
我觉得你对这件事应该就算了吧
I'm thinking you might have to let this one go.

108
00:04:38,570 --> 00:04:40,170
"算了吧"
Ugh, "Let it go."

109
00:04:40,170 --> 00:04:41,880
这句话我听了一辈子了
I have heard that my whole life.

110
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:44,660
每次我有事情不开心  就有人让我"算了吧"
Every time something upsets me somebody says, "Let it go,"

111
00:04:44,660 --> 00:04:46,060
说得好像都是我的问题
you know, like it's my fault,

112
00:04:46,060 --> 00:04:48,340
我有不高兴的情绪是不对的
and it's not okay to feel the way I feel.

113
00:04:48,340 --> 00:04:49,560
我不知道该说什么了
I don't know what to tell you.

114
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:51,150
你何不跟她谈谈呢
I mean, why don't you talk to her?

115
00:04:51,790 --> 00:04:53,130
你就这点能耐吗
Is that all you have?

116
00:04:53,130 --> 00:04:56,240
"跟她谈"和"算了吧"这种陈腔滥调的方法招数
Shopworn tidbits like "talk to her" and "let it go"?

117
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:58,320
佩妮  生活给了我又酸又苦的柠檬
Gee, Penny, life's giving me lemons.

118
00:04:58,320 --> 00:04:59,390
我该怎么办
What should I do?

119
00:04:59,390 --> 00:05:02,030
你可以找个"地方"塞进去呀
Well, you could shove them somewhere.

120
00:05:03,950 --> 00:05:06,440
好吧  现在你会发散思维了
Okay, now you're getting creative.

121
00:05:08,190 --> 00:05:09,630
再次感谢你们来帮忙
Thanks again for your help.

122
00:05:09,630 --> 00:05:10,670
-不用谢  -别客气
- No problem. - Our pleasure.

123
00:05:10,670 --> 00:05:12,000
这地方看起来真棒
The place really looks great.

124
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:14,600
是啊  你应该早几年放火烧掉的
Yeah, you should have burned it down years ago.

125
00:05:15,590 --> 00:05:17,830
我再三地告诉你们  不是我故意烧掉的
I keep telling you I didn't burn it down.

126
00:05:17,830 --> 00:05:19,390
我们知道  因为为了骗保险金
We know, we know-- because burning something down

127
00:05:19,390 --> 00:05:22,930
而故意纵火  那叫"犯罪"
for the insurance money is a "crime."

128
00:05:24,440 --> 00:05:26,810
斯尔图特  这地方简直焕然一新呀
Stuart, this place looks amazing.

129
00:05:26,810 --> 00:05:27,830
谢谢
Thanks.

130
00:05:27,830 --> 00:05:29,580
看得出来你很用心
You really did a nice job.

131
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:32,360
谢谢你在这整段过程中
And thank you for putting up with me

132
00:05:32,360 --> 00:05:34,020
容忍我住在你妈家里
staying at your mom's through all this.

133
00:05:34,020 --> 00:05:36,200
否则我也不能重开这家店
I-I couldn't have done it otherwise.

134
00:05:36,200 --> 00:05:39,520
别说客套话了  我很高兴你能...
I appreciate that, and I'm glad you were able to...

135
00:05:40,820 --> 00:05:42,860
那是我妈的家具吗
Is that my mother's furniture?

136
00:05:44,930 --> 00:05:46,400
是啊  她说我可以搬过来用
Yeah, she said I could use it.

137
00:05:46,400 --> 00:05:48,040
看起来很搭吧
Doesn't it look great?

138
00:05:48,040 --> 00:05:52,300
还是放小房间里比较搭  因为它只属于那里
Not as great as it looks in the den where it belongs.

139
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:53,030
华仔
Howie.

140
00:05:53,030 --> 00:05:55,620
你何不索性把整个房间都搬空算了
Why don't you just clean out the whole room?

141
00:05:55,620 --> 00:05:58,190
把我三年级给我妈做的手工彩线小丑拿走啊
Take the string art clown I made her in third grade

142
00:05:58,190 --> 00:05:59,370
再随便把我参加游泳班
and the ribbon I got in swim class

143
00:05:59,370 --> 00:06:01,570
在水里憋气赢来的缎带奖拿走啊
for putting my face in the water.

144
00:06:01,570 --> 00:06:02,900
你干嘛生气啊
What is your problem?

145
00:06:02,900 --> 00:06:04,110
你妈都不介意了
She said it was okay.

146
00:06:04,110 --> 00:06:06,750
我是她的儿子  我很介意
Well, I'm her son, and I say it's not okay.

147
00:06:06,750 --> 00:06:11,270
哪门子的儿子  那手工小丑你也就花了十分钟做的吧
Some son-- looks like you spent ten minutes on that clown art.

148
00:06:12,170 --> 00:06:14,030
或许我应该像你一样去念名牌艺术学校
Well, maybe I should've gone to a fancy art school like you.

149
00:06:14,030 --> 00:06:15,570
然后开一家失败的漫画店
Then I could run a failed comic shop

150
00:06:15,570 --> 00:06:17,960
店倒了就去骗其他人妈妈的钱
and mooch off some guy's mother.

151
00:06:18,830 --> 00:06:20,640
我们先走吧  让你冷静一下
Why don't we leave so you can cool off?

152
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:22,380
这主意不错
I think that's a good idea.

153
00:06:22,380 --> 00:06:23,550
快带他离开我的店
Take him out of my store.

154
00:06:23,550 --> 00:06:24,330
你的店
Your store?!

155
00:06:24,330 --> 00:06:26,280
你重开店的钱还是我妈给的
My mother gave you the money to reopen.

156
00:06:26,280 --> 00:06:27,620
我哪儿也不去
I'm not going anywhere.

157
00:06:27,620 --> 00:06:30,080
要不我们去给派对买点吃的吧
Why don't we go get the food for the party.

158
00:06:30,080 --> 00:06:31,170
麻烦你们了
Thank you.

159
00:06:31,170 --> 00:06:33,530
聪明  这样看起来我们好像在帮忙
Smart-- looks like we're being helpful.

160
00:06:33,530 --> 00:06:37,140
其实我们只是想快点逃离这个难堪的场面
Mmm, when really we're just exiting an uncomfortable situation.

161
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:42,520
为什么偏偏要帮巴里·克里普奇呢
Kripke, you know, of all the people-- Barry Kripke.

162
00:06:42,520 --> 00:06:44,510
我超....你是故意像个疯子一样叠衣服
I'm so... Are you folding it like a crazy person

163
00:06:44,510 --> 00:06:46,520
好让我看不过眼帮你吗
to get me to do it for you?!

164
00:06:47,680 --> 00:06:48,900
不是啊
No.

165
00:06:50,810 --> 00:06:52,450
算了  我来吧
Oh, give me that.

166
00:06:58,050 --> 00:07:00,220
我很好奇
Just out of curiosity,

167
00:07:00,220 --> 00:07:03,190
如果我想放下某件事
if I were to let something go,

168
00:07:03,190 --> 00:07:04,800
我该怎么做到呢
how would I do that?

169
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:07,610
我不知道  想想其他事情试试
I don't know-- just think about something else.

170
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:10,880
我可以想食蚁兽吗
Can I think about the spiny anteater?

171
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:12,000
可以啊
Sure.

172
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:14,740
食蚁兽
The spiny anteater...

173
00:07:14,740 --> 00:07:18,020
从来没背着我去帮忙巴里·克里普奇
never went behind my back and worked with Barry Kripke.

174
00:07:19,650 --> 00:07:22,220
这招一点用都没有
That didn't help at all.

175
00:07:22,700 --> 00:07:25,380
有些人会尝试运用观想术
You know, some people try visualization.

176
00:07:25,380 --> 00:07:27,010
那要怎么做
How does that work?

177
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:29,540
好
Okay,

178
00:07:30,860 --> 00:07:33,810
想象你的问题是一支笔
imagine your problems are a pen.

179
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:36,410
好的
Okay.

180
00:07:36,410 --> 00:07:39,560
现在想象你握着那支笔
Now imagine you're holding that pen.

181
00:07:44,170 --> 00:07:45,800
好的
Okay.

182
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:49,060
现在松开手  让笔掉下来[算了吧]
Now open your hand and let it go.

183
00:07:49,060 --> 00:07:51,130
可我才拿到这支笔
But I just got this pen.

184
00:07:52,280 --> 00:07:55,050
上面有我名字的首字母缩写呢
It's got my initials on it and everything.

185
00:07:55,050 --> 00:07:56,560
你看
Look.

186
00:07:58,860 --> 00:08:01,510
谢尔顿  这没有那么难
Sheldon, this isn't that hard.

187
00:08:03,630 --> 00:08:05,910
我或许有个让你教我的更好办法
I may have a better way that you can teach me.

188
00:08:05,910 --> 00:08:07,080
怎么做
How?

189
00:08:07,720 --> 00:08:10,840
如果我告诉你  在过去几个月里
What if I told you that over the past few months

190
00:08:10,840 --> 00:08:13,750
艾米在暗中悄悄让你做一些智力小难题
Amy has secretly been giving you little puzzles

191
00:08:13,750 --> 00:08:17,930
就为了对比你和她实验室黑猩猩谁更聪明
to test your intelligence against chimpanzees in her lab?

192
00:08:19,290 --> 00:08:21,300
什么  她才没让我解决什么小难题呢
What? She didn't give me any puzzles.

193
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:23,300
你确定吗
Are you sure?

194
00:08:25,720 --> 00:08:29,250
天啊  我把剪刀弄成两半装不回来了
Boy, I just can't seem to get these scissors back together.

195
00:08:29,250 --> 00:08:30,920
你能帮个忙吗
Can you do it?

196
00:08:32,980 --> 00:08:33,860
糟糕
Darn it.

197
00:08:33,860 --> 00:08:35,830
我的眼睛进东西了
There's something in my eye,

198
00:08:35,830 --> 00:08:38,610
我得把这些硬币按大小分类
and I need to sort these coins by size.

199
00:08:38,610 --> 00:08:40,180
你能帮个忙吗
Can you help?

200
00:08:46,380 --> 00:08:47,200
佩妮
Penny?

201
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:49,800
我超级想吃香蕉
I really want to eat this banana,

202
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:53,780
但它被卡在这个竹子机关箱了
but it's stuck inside this bamboo puzzle box.

203
00:08:55,560 --> 00:08:58,050
那个科学婊
Son of a bitch!

204
00:08:58,720 --> 00:08:59,700
太好了
Okay, that's great.

205
00:08:59,700 --> 00:09:03,670
现在想  算了吧
Now, let it go.

206
00:09:07,160 --> 00:09:10,170
你们居然把我和黑猩猩拿来做测试对比
I can't believe you were testing me against a chimp!

207
00:09:10,170 --> 00:09:12,730
抱歉  测试你的人是艾米
Well, excuse me, Amy was testing you.

208
00:09:12,730 --> 00:09:15,470
我可是很看好你哦
I was rooting for you.

209
00:09:16,430 --> 00:09:19,570
对了  打开机关箱那次做得很不错哟
Good job on that banana box, by the way.

210
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:22,070
她为什么要这样做
Why would she even do this?

211
00:09:22,070 --> 00:09:24,290
艾米在对人猿进行一系列实验
She's been conducting an experiment on apes

212
00:09:24,290 --> 00:09:26,540
给它们各种难题  让它们解决
where they're given various puzzles to solve.

213
00:09:26,540 --> 00:09:29,180
我对难题的复杂度表示惊讶
I was surprised at the complexity of the puzzles

214
00:09:29,180 --> 00:09:31,410
觉得可能有些人类都未必能解决
and thought some humans wouldn't be able to solve them.

215
00:09:31,410 --> 00:09:34,730
于是艾米就说  "想让实验变得更有趣吗"
That's when Amy said, "Want to make this interesting?"

216
00:09:35,820 --> 00:09:37,300
"让实验变得有趣"
"Make this interesting"?

217
00:09:37,300 --> 00:09:38,820
你们还拿我开赌盘了吗
You bet money on me?

218
00:09:38,820 --> 00:09:40,080
当然不
No, no.

219
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:42,780
我们设计了让你参与其中的实验
We designed an experiment involving you.

220
00:09:42,780 --> 00:09:45,150
瞧  这样是不是很有趣呀
See? Now, isn't that interesting?

221
00:09:46,250 --> 00:09:47,650
这一点都不有趣
It's not interesting.

222
00:09:47,650 --> 00:09:49,480
简直太侮辱人了
It's incredibly insulting.

223
00:09:49,480 --> 00:09:51,820
好吧  或许这样会有用
Okay, maybe this will help--

224
00:09:51,820 --> 00:09:54,570
想象你拿着一支笔
imagine you're holding a pen.

225
00:09:55,790 --> 00:09:58,680
别想太多  就是一支普通的笔
Before you go too far, not a special pen

226
00:09:58,680 --> 00:10:00,240
上面没有刻你的姓名首字母
with your initials engraved on it--

227
00:10:00,240 --> 00:10:01,610
不然下一步会很难做
that'll make the next part really hard.

228
00:10:02,950 --> 00:10:03,630
够了
That's it.

229
00:10:03,630 --> 00:10:04,670
出去
Get out!

230
00:10:04,670 --> 00:10:06,830
我不懂你为啥要冲我发火
I don't understand why you're mad at me.

231
00:10:06,830 --> 00:10:08,400
你应该朝艾米发火
You should be mad at Amy.

232
00:10:08,400 --> 00:10:10,400
跟我下午的时候一样
Like I was this afternoon.

233
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:12,490
你瞧  我已经算了
Hey, look at that-- I let it go.

234
00:10:12,490 --> 00:10:13,580
出去
Get out!

235
00:10:16,450 --> 00:10:18,350
-佩妮  -干嘛
- Penny? - What?

236
00:10:18,810 --> 00:10:20,850
我好像把笔留在里面了
I think I left my pen in there.

237
00:10:24,420 --> 00:10:26,020
我懂你为什么不开心
I understand why you're upset,

238
00:10:26,020 --> 00:10:28,450
可是他真的很努力地准备开店
but he worked really hard to get the store ready.

239
00:10:28,450 --> 00:10:30,930
不过是一些家具
And it's just furniture.

240
00:10:30,930 --> 00:10:32,720
是我妈的家具
It's my mom's furniture.

241
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:34,370
属于我从小长大的房子
It belongs in the house I grew up in--

242
00:10:34,370 --> 00:10:36,140
就放在那堆电视节目表旁边
next to that pile of TV Guides

243
00:10:36,140 --> 00:10:38,870
在一个十岁孩子的眼里
and in plain view of what, for a ten-year-old,

244
00:10:38,870 --> 00:10:41,170
可是很棒的线条艺术
was a quality piece of string art!

245
00:10:44,150 --> 00:10:45,760
华仔  等漫画店成功
Howie, if the store succeeds,

246
00:10:45,760 --> 00:10:47,130
斯图尔特有了收入
Stuart has a source of income,

247
00:10:47,130 --> 00:10:49,060
他就能搬出你妈的房子
and he can move out of your mother's house.

248
00:10:49,060 --> 00:10:51,030
付出这些旧家具作为代价
Seems like some old furniture is a reasonable price

249
00:10:51,030 --> 00:10:52,880
还是挺划算的
to pay for that.

250
00:10:53,520 --> 00:10:54,760
这倒是个好理由
That is a good point.

251
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:56,230
可是我跟你结婚不是为了好理由
But I didn't marry you for good points.

252
00:10:56,230 --> 00:10:57,460
我跟你结婚是为了
I married you to blindly support me

253
00:10:57,460 --> 00:11:00,120
不管我有多荒谬  你都会盲目支持我
no matter how ridiculous I'm being!

254
00:11:01,900 --> 00:11:05,010
所以我才改写了我们的结婚誓言啊
This is why I had to rewrite our wedding vows.

255
00:11:09,520 --> 00:11:11,820
你好  我们来拿漫画中心订的餐
Hi, we're here to pick up an order for Comic Center.

256
00:11:11,820 --> 00:11:14,110
好  让我查一下
Sure, let me go check on that.

257
00:11:15,100 --> 00:11:18,850
我觉得那是内森·菲利安
Dude, I-I think that's Nathan Fillion.

258
00:11:19,340 --> 00:11:21,820
真的是他
Oh yeah, look at that.

259
00:11:21,820 --> 00:11:23,870
他正在挑掉番茄里的沙拉
And he's picking the tomatoes out of his salad

260
00:11:23,870 --> 00:11:25,580
跟我一样
just like I do.

261
00:11:26,090 --> 00:11:28,390
我一直觉得自己跟他有缘
I always did feel a connection with him.

262
00:11:30,240 --> 00:11:31,550
我有个主意
Oh, I have got an idea.

263
00:11:31,550 --> 00:11:35,010
我们不会去拍卖网站上卖他的番茄
We're not selling his tomatoes on eBay.

264
00:11:35,010 --> 00:11:38,830
如果我们能让《萤火虫》里的雷诺兹船长
No, if we got Captain Reynolds from Firefly

265
00:11:38,830 --> 00:11:41,030
去斯图尔特的店办签名会
to do a signing at Stuart's store,

266
00:11:41,030 --> 00:11:42,510
那一定超棒
that would be amazing.

267
00:11:42,510 --> 00:11:43,970
一定很棒
That would be great.

268
00:11:43,970 --> 00:11:45,890
所以我们要过去搭话吗
So should we go talk to him?

269
00:11:45,890 --> 00:11:47,140
我不知道
I don't know.

270
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:49,450
如果他态度不好  以后他演的剧
I mean, if he's not nice, it's gonna make it hard for me

271
00:11:49,450 --> 00:11:51,860
-我就没法看了  -屁咧
- to watch him in anything again. - What?!

272
00:11:51,860 --> 00:11:54,600
演琼恩·雪诺的是个混蛋
The-the guy who plays Jon Snow was a jerk.

273
00:11:54,600 --> 00:11:56,120
我们还是在看《权利的游戏》啊
We still watch Game of Thrones.

274
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:59,020
他是混蛋是因为你追了他的尾
He was a jerk because you rear-ended him.

275
00:11:59,730 --> 00:12:01,370
我注意力被分散了嘛
I was distracted.

276
00:12:01,370 --> 00:12:03,410
一个守夜人的车上绑着皮划艇
It's weird seeing a member of the Night's Watch

277
00:12:03,410 --> 00:12:05,210
确实很奇怪嘛
with a kayak strapped to his car.

278
00:12:07,110 --> 00:12:08,040
来吧
Come on.

279
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:13,790
你好 抱歉
Hi, excuse me, s-s...

280
00:12:13,790 --> 00:12:15,260
我们不想打扰您
I-I don't mean to bother you,

281
00:12:15,260 --> 00:12:18,200
可我们真的非常喜欢《萤火虫》
but we're just really big fans of Firefly.

282
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:20,010
还有《恐怖博士》
A-And Dr. Horrible.

283
00:12:20,010 --> 00:12:21,990
你们认错人了
Oh, uh, I think you made a mistake.

284
00:12:21,990 --> 00:12:23,640
我不是演员
I'm not an actor.

285
00:12:23,640 --> 00:12:25,540
别这么说
Don't say that.

286
00:12:25,540 --> 00:12:27,070
虽然没到朱迪·丹奇女爵士的等级
I mean, you're not Dame Judi Dench,

287
00:12:25,540 --> 00:12:29,020
知名英国女演员  曾获英国电影学院终身成就奖

288
00:12:27,070 --> 00:12:29,020
但你也挺不错的
but you're pretty great.

289
00:12:32,150 --> 00:12:34,360
我懂了  你们以为我是内森·菲利安
Oh, yeah, I get it-- you think I'm Nathan Fillion,

290
00:12:32,150 --> 00:12:35,250
知名男演员  曾出演《萤火虫》《灵书妙探》

291
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:35,250
可我不是
but I'm not.

292
00:12:35,250 --> 00:12:38,840
你们要是不介意  我想继续吃午饭了
So if you don't mind, I would just love to eat my lunch.

293
00:12:39,290 --> 00:12:40,150
走吧
Come on.

294
00:12:40,150 --> 00:12:41,970
很抱歉打扰您了
Sorry to bother you.

295
00:12:41,970 --> 00:12:44,430
真不懂他脾气怎么这么差
Don't know why he's so grumpy.

296
00:12:44,430 --> 00:12:46,460
上次有人误以为我演了《少年派》
I got mistaken for that guy in Life of Pi once,

297
00:12:44,430 --> 00:12:46,460
该电影男主角是另一位印度演员

298
00:12:46,460 --> 00:12:49,070
我到现在还飘飘然呢
and I'm still floating.

299
00:12:52,090 --> 00:12:53,840
谢尔顿  是我
Sheldon, it's me.

300
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:55,120
你好
Oh, hey.

301
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:57,080
你看到了吗
D-Did you see that?

302
00:12:57,080 --> 00:13:01,470
我自己找出了开门的方法
I-I figured out how to open the door all by myself.

303
00:13:02,630 --> 00:13:07,140
我是不是该在笼子里扔粪庆祝啊
Maybe I'll fling some feces around my cage to celebrate.

304
00:13:08,020 --> 00:13:09,490
你在说什么
What are you talking about?

305
00:13:09,490 --> 00:13:12,630
我知道你秘密拿我做实验
I know you've been giving me secret puzzle tests.

306
00:13:14,990 --> 00:13:16,660
谢尔顿  开门
Sheldon, open the door.

307
00:13:16,660 --> 00:13:18,320
我不能开
I can't.

308
00:13:18,330 --> 00:13:20,630
我光着呢
I'm naked.

309
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:23,470
我刚看到你了
I just saw you.

310
00:13:23,470 --> 00:13:25,390
等一下
Hang on.

311
00:13:26,080 --> 00:13:28,380
现在开门
Open the door now.

312
00:13:28,380 --> 00:13:30,790
把裤子穿上
Pull up your pants!

313
00:13:33,120 --> 00:13:34,660
这没什么大不了的
It's not a big deal.

314
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:37,520
我本科的时候经常做这种实验
I run tests like this on undergrads all the time.

315
00:13:37,520 --> 00:13:39,250
如果你在大学里填写一些问卷
If you fill out some paperwork at the university,

316
00:13:39,250 --> 00:13:41,550
我可以给你五块钱
I can get you $5.

317
00:13:41,550 --> 00:13:43,220
谁稀罕你的五块钱
I don't want $5.

318
00:13:43,220 --> 00:13:45,400
我要的是尊严
I want my dignity.

319
00:13:46,150 --> 00:13:48,180
那你到底要多少  十块吗
So what are we talking, like, ten bucks?

320
00:13:50,290 --> 00:13:52,380
-谢谢  -谢谢
- Thank you. - Thanks.

321
00:13:54,260 --> 00:13:56,160
-再次抱歉  -没关系
- Sorry again. - No problem.

322
00:13:56,610 --> 00:13:58,820
你确定你不是他吗
A-Are you sure you're not him?

323
00:13:58,820 --> 00:14:00,120
你可以告诉我们的
Uh, you can tell us.

324
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:03,420
我们是科学家  不是什么狂热粉
We're scientists, not crazy fanboys.

325
00:14:04,710 --> 00:14:06,390
好吧
All right, fine.

326
00:14:06,390 --> 00:14:07,900
我就是他
I'm him.

327
00:14:07,900 --> 00:14:11,210
结果你自己一个人在熟食店吃饭吗
And you're eating alone at a deli.

328
00:14:11,210 --> 00:14:13,760
我不信  你不是他
I don't buy it-- you're not him.

329
00:14:14,750 --> 00:14:16,580
我就想安静地吃个午饭
I just wanted to eat my lunch in peace.

330
00:14:16,580 --> 00:14:17,750
不过我确实是他
But I really am him.

331
00:14:17,750 --> 00:14:19,850
多谢你们能成为我的粉丝
And thank you very much for being a fan.

332
00:14:19,850 --> 00:14:21,690
你们要是想可以跟我合照
If you want, uh, let's take a picture.

333
00:14:22,170 --> 00:14:23,210
-那太好了  -好啊
- That would be great. - Great.

334
00:14:23,210 --> 00:14:25,160
-谢谢  -当然
- Yeah, thank you. - You bet.

335
00:14:28,930 --> 00:14:30,520
等等
Wait, hang on.

336
00:14:31,750 --> 00:14:34,110
如果你真的是内森·菲利安
If you're really Nathan Fillion,

337
00:14:34,110 --> 00:14:37,440
《萤火虫》里关于你帽子那句台词是什么
what's the line from Firefly about your bonnet?

338
00:14:38,270 --> 00:14:41,410
"以我美丽的花帽子起誓  我要了结了你"
"I swear by my pretty floral bonnet, I will end you."

339
00:14:42,820 --> 00:14:44,730
没错  就是这句
That's it, that's the line.

340
00:14:44,730 --> 00:14:46,160
不过...
Although...

341
00:14:46,160 --> 00:14:49,590
我也知道台词  但我也不是内森·菲利安啊
I knew the line-- doesn't make me Nathan Fillion.

342
00:14:50,890 --> 00:14:52,390
你到底想不想拍照了
Do you want the picture or not?

343
00:14:52,390 --> 00:14:55,270
我想和内森·菲利安拍照
I want a picture with Nathan Fillion.

344
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:58,480
跟一个长的像内森·菲利安  但是要比
How about a picture with a guy who looks like Nathan Fillion

345
00:14:58,480 --> 00:15:01,970
平时的内森·菲利安更暴走一点的人呢
but a little more annoyed than Nathan Fillion usually is?

346
00:15:04,490 --> 00:15:06,080
你怎么说
What do you think?

347
00:15:06,730 --> 00:15:08,860
放脸书上是够了
Eh, it's good enough for Facebook.

348
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:17,640
不敢相信他们居然那么做
I can't believe they did that.

349
00:15:17,650 --> 00:15:19,650
我知道  太侮辱人了
I know-- it's so insulting.

350
00:15:19,650 --> 00:15:21,340
有一次  他们还让我把香蕉
At one point, they had me figure out

351
00:15:21,340 --> 00:15:24,690
从一个机关盒里拿出来
how to get a banana out of a puzzle box.

352
00:15:24,690 --> 00:15:27,290
等等  谢尔顿也给过我香蕉盒
Wait, Sheldon gave me a banana in a box.

353
00:15:27,290 --> 00:15:29,490
他也在测试我
He was testing me, too.

354
00:15:30,230 --> 00:15:31,420
难以置信
Unbelievable.

355
00:15:31,420 --> 00:15:33,410
而且黑猩猩怎么可能打开嘛
And how could a chimp even solve that?

356
00:15:33,410 --> 00:15:35,050
根本不可能
That was impossible.

357
00:15:35,050 --> 00:15:37,660
真的吗  你没拿出来吗
Really? You couldn't get it out?

358
00:15:40,800 --> 00:15:42,140
谢谢
Thank you.

359
00:15:42,140 --> 00:15:44,140
这商店太棒了
Wow, the store looks great.

360
00:15:44,140 --> 00:15:46,140
你们对我俩都做测试了吗
So you guys were testing us both?

361
00:15:46,140 --> 00:15:47,170
你们脑子有啥毛病啊
What is the matter with you?

362
00:15:47,180 --> 00:15:48,690
他们的毛病就是
Eh, what's the matter with them is

363
00:15:48,690 --> 00:15:50,280
他们觉得自己聪明到冒烟了
they think they're so smart they don't care

364
00:15:50,280 --> 00:15:51,940
根本不在乎会伤到别人的感情
if they hurt other people's feelings.

365
00:15:51,950 --> 00:15:54,200
-好像是这么回事  -完全不是这么回事
- Sounds like us. - That's not true.

366
00:15:56,830 --> 00:15:58,950
我还是没理解你们为什么生气
I still don't understand why you're upset.

367
00:15:58,950 --> 00:16:01,950
你们每道题都解的比黑猩猩快
You solved every puzzle faster than all of the chimps.

368
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:05,110
除了比巴纳巴斯慢  但他吃着药呢
Well, except Barnabas, but he was on Adderall.

369
00:16:06,780 --> 00:16:08,770
对不起  可是逼得我快疯了
I'm sorry, but it's making me crazy.

370
00:16:08,770 --> 00:16:10,930
你能不能就这么算了吧
Can you please just let it go?

371
00:16:10,930 --> 00:16:13,220
这事我能帮忙
Oh, I can help you with that.

372
00:16:14,190 --> 00:16:17,700
想象你手里握着一支普通的笔
Imagine you're holding an ordinary pen.

373
00:16:18,510 --> 00:16:22,750
而你最喜欢地笔好好的放在口袋里
While your favorite pen is safe and secure in your pocket.

374
00:16:24,940 --> 00:16:25,970
等会再说
Hold that thought.

375
00:16:26,780 --> 00:16:27,820
你好
Hello?

376
00:16:27,820 --> 00:16:29,960
要怎么才能弥补
How can I make this up to you?

377
00:16:29,960 --> 00:16:32,070
答案就在这个机关盒里
The answer's in this puzzle box.

378
00:16:32,070 --> 00:16:34,650
看看你能不能打开它呢
Let's see if you can open it.

379
00:16:38,070 --> 00:16:40,420
你就不能先提醒他一下家具的事吗
You could have at least warned him about the furniture.

380
00:16:40,420 --> 00:16:42,450
我们搬的时候  我就是这么说的
That's what I said when we moved it.

381
00:16:42,450 --> 00:16:43,890
你还帮着搬了
You helped him?!

382
00:16:43,890 --> 00:16:47,360
没有  抱枕都是斯图尔特自己搬的哦
No, Stuart picked out those throw pillows all on his own.

383
00:16:51,220 --> 00:16:53,010
你没事吧
Hey, you okay?

384
00:16:53,700 --> 00:16:54,830
有事
Uh, no.

385
00:16:54,830 --> 00:16:56,060
怎么了
What's wrong?

386
00:16:57,810 --> 00:17:00,250
我母亲去世了
My mom died.

387
00:16:57,810 --> 00:17:01,840
为霍华德母亲配音的演员已在2014年11月11日去世了

388
00:17:00,250 --> 00:17:01,840
什么
What?

389
00:17:04,590 --> 00:17:07,460
是我姨妈打来的
That was my aunt.

390
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:09,580
妈妈小睡了一会
Ma took a nap.

391
00:17:10,270 --> 00:17:12,620
但她再也没醒过来
She never woke up.

392
00:17:13,190 --> 00:17:15,740
天啊  华仔
Oh, my God, Howie.

393
00:17:17,880 --> 00:17:19,700
节哀
I'm so sorry.

394
00:17:20,710 --> 00:17:22,220
我们能帮上什么吗
What can we do?

395
00:17:24,780 --> 00:17:26,770
不知道
I don't know.

396
00:17:31,660 --> 00:17:32,890
我能说句话吗
May I say something?

397
00:17:32,890 --> 00:17:34,220
时机不对  谢尔顿
Not right now, Sheldon.

398
00:17:34,220 --> 00:17:35,820
-但我觉得可以安慰到他  -兄弟
- But I think it would be comforting. - Buddy...

399
00:17:35,820 --> 00:17:37,760
不  没事的
No, it's okay.

400
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:39,910
你想说什么
What?

401
00:17:40,280 --> 00:17:42,950
当我的父亲去世时
When I lost my own father,

402
00:17:42,950 --> 00:17:45,710
我没有任何朋友陪我渡过那段时间
I didn't have any friends to help me through it.

403
00:17:47,230 --> 00:17:48,580
而你有
You do.

404
00:17:54,340 --> 00:17:58,100
我真以为他会说"算了吧"
I really thought he was gonna say, "let it go."

405
00:18:05,290 --> 00:18:06,860
谢谢  伯纳黛特
Okay, thanks, Bernadette.

406
00:18:06,860 --> 00:18:08,840
一路平安
Travel safe.

407
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:10,830
好  再见
Okay, bye.

408
00:18:11,950 --> 00:18:13,110
他们订了机票
They booked a flight.

409
00:18:13,110 --> 00:18:14,860
现在往机场走呢
They're heading to the airport now.

410
00:18:14,860 --> 00:18:16,530
霍华德状态怎么样
How's Howard holding up?

411
00:18:16,530 --> 00:18:18,010
他还撑得住
He's hanging in there.

412
00:18:18,010 --> 00:18:20,500
你还好吗  斯图尔特
How are you doing, Stuart?

413
00:18:21,360 --> 00:18:22,790
还是不敢相信她居然走了
Still can't believe she's gone.

414
00:18:22,790 --> 00:18:25,550
是这个女人收留了我
I mean, that woman took me in.

415
00:18:25,550 --> 00:18:28,580
如果没有她  我可能要露宿街头了
If it wasn't for her, I-I would have been homeless.

416
00:18:28,580 --> 00:18:30,420
我们中也肯定有人会收留你的
One of us would have taken you in.

417
00:18:30,420 --> 00:18:33,070
是吗  我怎么没想起来有谁说过
Yeah, I don't recall any offers.

418
00:18:34,160 --> 00:18:37,090
但这样也挺好  我很高兴最后是她收留了我
But, you know, uh, I-I'm glad it worked out the way it did

419
00:18:37,090 --> 00:18:41,480
因为我由此认识了一位善良的人
because I got to know this wonderful person.

420
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:42,880
是啊
Yeah.

421
00:18:42,880 --> 00:18:45,060
沃罗威茨夫人非常特别
Mrs. Wolowitz was pretty special.

422
00:18:45,060 --> 00:18:47,010
当我刚搬到美国
When I first moved to America,

423
00:18:47,010 --> 00:18:49,540
那时霍华德是我唯一的朋友
Howard was my only friend.

424
00:18:49,540 --> 00:18:52,780
她让我在她家时宾至如归
She made me feel so welcome in her home.

425
00:18:52,780 --> 00:18:55,780
不过事出有因  因为那几年
Which says a lot, because, those first few years,

426
00:18:55,780 --> 00:18:58,020
她一直以为我是她家园丁
she thought I was the gardener.

427
00:19:00,300 --> 00:19:01,220
她每次见到我
Whenever I saw her,

428
00:19:01,220 --> 00:19:05,230
都说我太瘦了  使劲让我多吃
she'd say I was too skinny and try and feed me.

429
00:19:06,110 --> 00:19:07,810
她也是这样对我的
She did that to me, too.

430
00:19:07,810 --> 00:19:10,480
别抢走我对她的独家回忆
Don't take this away from me.

431
00:19:11,640 --> 00:19:14,050
我不介意她的大吼大叫
I didn't care for her yelling.

432
00:19:14,520 --> 00:19:17,050
但现在我再也听不到了
But now that I'm not going to hear it again,

433
00:19:17,050 --> 00:19:18,680
真伤心
I'm sad.

434
00:19:18,680 --> 00:19:21,360
你要是乐意  之后我可以吼你
If you want, I can yell at you later.

435
00:19:23,210 --> 00:19:25,260
你吼不出她的霸气
It won't be as good.

436
00:19:27,550 --> 00:19:29,120
我们举杯
Let's have a toast.

437
00:19:31,050 --> 00:19:33,260
敬沃罗威茨夫人
To Mrs. Wolowitz.

438
00:19:33,780 --> 00:19:35,620
我们所有人亲爱的...
A loving mother...

439
00:19:38,230 --> 00:19:40,540
母亲
...to all of us.

440
00:19:41,760 --> 00:19:43,480
我们会想念您
We'll miss you.

